<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>\mathbf{a} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -5 \\ 6 \end{array}\right)}</m>, <m>\mathbf{b} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 1 \\ 3 \end{array}\right)}</m> and <m>\mathbf{c} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 2 \\ -5 \end{array}\right)}</m>.</p><p>(a) Find <m>\mathbf{a} + \mathbf{b}</m>.</p><div><m>\mathbf{a} + \mathbf{b} =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Find <m>\mathbf{a} + \mathbf{b} + \mathbf{c}</m>.</p><div><m>\mathbf{a} + \mathbf{b} + \mathbf{c} =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="ans2"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Add across with across and up with up.</p><p>(a) Top: <m>{-5} + {1} = {-4}</m>. Bottom: <m>{6} + {3} = {9}</m>. So <m>\mathbf{a} + \mathbf{b} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -4 \\ 9 \end{array}\right)}</m>.</p><p>(b) Add <m>\mathbf{c}</m> to your answer to (a): <m>{\left(\begin{array}{c} -4 \\ 9 \end{array}\right)} + {\left(\begin{array}{c} 2 \\ -5 \end{array}\right)} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -2 \\ 4 \end{array}\right)}</m>.</p><p>Drawn head to tail, the resultant goes from the tail of <m>\mathbf{a}</m> to the head of the last vector.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left(\begin{array}{c} -4 \\ 9 \end{array}\right)</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\left(\begin{array}{c} -2 \\ 4 \end{array}\right)</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>